  "review": {
    "entityID": "place:babylon_151",
    "book": "2KI",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2KI 17:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "The king of Assyria brought people from Babylon, from Cuthah, from Avva, and from Hamath and Sepharvaim, and placed them in the cities of Samaria instead of the children of Israel; and they possessed Samaria and lived in its cities.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "eddaf8260d69ed6807531458f060562726957a926eba1ec54dbf2c7a13605404",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI17.htm#V24"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 17:30",
        "textualBasisJa": "The men of Babylon made Succoth Benoth, and the men of Cuth made Nergal, and the men of Hamath made Ashima,",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "1a7d69bea833a8b11b086054737a6f221c3c0c549712437a3657e0f035212fc6",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI17.htm#V30"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "At that time Berodach Baladan the son of Baladan, king of Babylon, sent letters and a present to Hezekiah, for he had heard that Hezekiah had been sick.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "e83d78abab0e4eae30d18a094f2ca3efbe11e97a908e4a5238d0373e23322433",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI20.htm#V12"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:14",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Isaiah the prophet came to King Hezekiah, and said to him, “What did these men say? From where did they come to you?” Hezekiah said, “They have come from a far country, even from Babylon.”",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "3c4347ba0b7d934675f5274532bedb068defd9a82dc6bea9e418f99f819ef058",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI20.htm#V14"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "‘Behold, the days come that all that is in your house, and that which your fathers have laid up in store to this day, will be carried to Babylon. Nothing will be left,’ says the LORD.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "73c88700ab9924580b4e6afc7d8860f18ef10ba283bf4d04648ac961713a6be8",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI20.htm#V17"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 20:18",
        "textualBasisJa": "‘They will take away some of your sons who will issue from you, whom you will father; and they will be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon.’”",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "3ef77661d47424b7a3e456191fb31e2091736d185af95f6286c4600b96104a59",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI20.htm#V18"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 24:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "In his days Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up, and Jehoiakim became his servant for three years. Then he turned and rebelled against him.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "5a8ad194bec78f3dffe0fc541ec7e042c3530aab633fb9d4150deee94e8c9080",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI24.htm#V1"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 24:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "The king of Egypt didn’t come out of his land any more; for the king of Babylon had taken, from the brook of Egypt to the river Euphrates, all that belonged to the king of Egypt.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "7885e293c030a9e7b55d6e421b072752ef4a13db0b8bdb69804466051b65d135",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI24.htm#V7"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 24:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "At that time the servants of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up to Jerusalem, and the city was besieged.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "71affb2660d63945f656e350152900c2e00430d1c70f5557152c06e3861ad7d8",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI24.htm#V10"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 24:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came to the city while his servants were besieging it,",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "ec16eed818ae3db4b4c6e726d2697636bbf84866f1a1da8dd411a347dc1d6922",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI24.htm#V11"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 24:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "and Jehoiachin the king of Judah went out to the king of Babylon—he, his mother, his servants, his princes, and his officers; and the king of Babylon captured him in the eighth year of his reign.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "80de5a5bdb7c3e136af26349c11fb4a8ccbb9996b7dd5237b3401f292b382f74",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI24.htm#V12"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 24:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "He carried away Jehoiachin to Babylon, with the king’s mother, the king’s wives, his officers, and the chief men of the land. He carried them into captivity from Jerusalem to Babylon.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "1cfec4a6fb99807957174f8668859649db5f8e0020a2b67aa4741f36eb67a783",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI24.htm#V15"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 24:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "All the men of might, even seven thousand, and the craftsmen and the smiths one thousand, all of them strong and fit for war, even them the king of Babylon brought captive to Babylon.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "1dcfdc0f69e2b26c45fa3c61cdbc90c9d2ea375887881044a751bdd017c4e2a4",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI24.htm#V16"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 24:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "The king of Babylon made Mattaniah, Jehoiachin’s father’s brother, king in his place, and changed his name to Zedekiah.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "48b888e922ce373610a755c5a6a26e40cf4f3b446e23b340725db46d5865ddb0",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI24.htm#V17"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 24:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "For through the anger of the LORD, this happened in Jerusalem and Judah, until he had cast them out from his presence. Then Zedekiah rebelled against the king of Babylon.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "f0023ab7120db1ac0c84de9a4568f278b3bb5e854d27fa84230e9855be587509",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI24.htm#V20"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "In the ninth year of his reign, in the tenth month, in the tenth day of the month, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came, he and all his army, against Jerusalem, and encamped against it; and they built forts against it around it.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "7ae781c1834e8995cbb47b2279ded16da1aa9faacbd7b1b213bb244a8efd6af8",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V1"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then they captured the king and carried him up to the king of Babylon to Riblah; and they passed judgment on him.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "5d0c98c9cd58364cbc7a98f31e049e9b490a75094d04936a1663b49219b795fa",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V6"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "They killed Zedekiah’s sons before his eyes, then put out Zedekiah’s eyes, bound him in fetters, and carried him to Babylon.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "667f1b7b68c8b7b0020673ca0910992b9a3c958f2cecefe27fd4a66c245aa751",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V7"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now in the fifth month, on the seventh day of the month, which was the nineteenth year of King Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard, a servant of the king of Babylon, came to Jerusalem.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "393371f0f8e0bf3636e2321d65ae63ac393812aea5c3b911f715bf391a2942bc",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V8"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard carried away captive the rest of the people who were left in the city and those who had deserted to the king of Babylon—all the rest of the multitude.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "99a55e779f427f107229f8e842635dde489fd869e60c3a5e49291c8d46254c45",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V11"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "The Chaldeans broke up the pillars of bronze that were in the LORD’s house and the bases and the bronze sea that were in the LORD’s house, and carried the bronze pieces to Babylon.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "23f4a58932f9437aaade08041b8368fbf1749152ae46f434a84a64d645c5ab93",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V13"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard took them, and brought them to the king of Babylon to Riblah.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "82d6a4a90ff2958c8ee7a296db5ac1d11a322ef7ff07a95d006a053e66ffd8dd",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V20"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "The king of Babylon attacked them and put them to death at Riblah in the land of Hamath. So Judah was carried away captive out of his land.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "75d4be91871f8bebd00305b9180da1b80e46951a5cba9054df64926e22f99daf",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V21"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "As for the people who were left in the land of Judah whom Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon had left, even over them he made Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, governor.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "bf9fbb77d6c3c7e8aa739813e94896c08b4a6245e808e0de7fd6e71ed9492927",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V22"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:23",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now when all the captains of the forces, they and their men, heard that the king of Babylon had made Gedaliah governor, they came to Gedaliah to Mizpah, even Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, Johanan the son of Kareah, Seraiah the son of Tanhumeth the Netophathite, and Jaazaniah the son of the Maacathite, they and their men.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "148c1967851582a771aa326d85e7d5a5b4cb0599e0760d55d64c6c396f387cfd",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V23"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "Gedaliah swore to them and to their men, and said to them, “Don’t be afraid because of the servants of the Chaldeans. Dwell in the land and serve the king of Babylon, and it will be well with you.”",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "cc44c705c58b798c3d8c578d4172775ccd62758520c38f64286f44213aad0faf",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V24"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:27",
        "textualBasisJa": "In the thirty-seventh year of the captivity of Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the twelfth month, on the twenty-seventh day of the month, Evilmerodach king of Babylon, in the year that he began to reign, released Jehoiachin king of Judah out of prison,",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "163c4b95efc90cadaa2202f495453a6f4bd549d63d4fa69742a7e0cfcf06c30c",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V27"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 25:28",
        "textualBasisJa": "and he spoke kindly to him and set his throne above the throne of the kings who were with him in Babylon,",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "56c7fab79b4d7711de57a306fd0c1bf04968ed55a670bce06f576b95894cfcfb",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI25.htm#V28"
      }
    ],
